certain basic principles, among which are these:
1. That it is the light which proceeds forth from the presence and
person of Deity to fill immensity, and that it is therefore everywhere
present;
2. That it is the agency of God's power, the law by which all things are
governed;
3. That it is the divine power which gives life to all things, and that if it
were completely withdrawn life would cease;
4. That it enlightens the mind and quickens the understanding of every
person born into the world (all have a conscience!);
5. That it strives with all men (the Holy Ghost testifies but does not
strive) unless and until they rebel against light and truth, at which time the
striving ceases, and in that sense the Spirit is withdrawn;
